  "ingredients": [
    "2.5 cups all-purpose flour",
    "0.25 cup packed brown sugar",
    "4 teaspoons baking powder",
    "2 teaspoons ground cinnamon",
    "1 teaspoon ground allspice",
    "1 teaspoon ground ginger",
    "0.5 teaspoon salt",
    "2 cups milk",
    "1 cup canned pumpkin",
    "4 eggs, separated",
    "0.25 cup butter, melted",
    "0.5 cup white sugar",
    "1 tablespoon cornstarch",
    "1 teaspoon ground cinnamon",
    "1 cup apple cider",
    "1 tablespoon lemon juice",
    "2 tablespoons butter"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat a waffle iron according to manufacturer's instructions.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine flour, brown sugar, baking powder, cinnamon, allspice, ginger, and salt in a mixing bowl. Stir milk, pumpkin, and egg yolks together in a separate bowl. Whip egg whites in a clean dry bowl until soft peaks form.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/b_nZR1FZ_dQcx7tU7n55ds_TWf0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/65691-Pumpkin-Waffles-With-Apple-Cider-Syrup-Step-1-0430-4b770cdc62aa437cb95a5197860431b3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/65691/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir flour mixture and 1/4 cup melted butter into pumpkin mixture just until combined. Fold 1/3 of the egg whites into the batter with a spatula until incorporated. Gently fold in remaining egg whites. Cook waffles in preheated waffle iron according to manufacturer's instructions.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IQjGUMqAphD0ZyhbjGFwZhCpJrU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/65691-Pumpkin-Waffles-With-Apple-Cider-Syrup-Step-3-0432-64786b2ef1234ab3a16bb8f0f1be4b43.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/65691/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the syrup: Stir sugar, cornstarch, and cinnamon together in a saucepan. Stir in apple cider and lemon juice. Cook over medium heat until mixture comes to a boil; continue boiling until thickened, about 2 minutes. Remove from heat and stir in 2 tablespoons of butter until melted. Serve waffles warm with apple cider syrup.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/mUekjs03Y3IM0WBQJN8PfJgxbHM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/65691-Pumpkin-Waffles-With-Apple-Cider-Syrup-Step-4-0436-6623304f00a949a3bfc36a56a46672a7.jpg"
      ],
